          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>The fibrous skeleton of the heart completely separates atrial and ventricular mu</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>The fibrous skeleton of the heart completely separates atrial and ventricular muscle. What is the sole pathway for electrical impulses to cross from the atria to the ventricles?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Purkinje fibres</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Purkinje fibres distribute impulses within the ventricular walls after the impulse has already crossed the fibrous skeleton. They do not bridge the gap between atria and ventricles.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Coronary sinus</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The coronary sinus is a venous channel returning deoxygenated blood to the right atrium. It plays no role in electrical conduction.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>AV node and Bundle of His</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The fibrous skeleton acts as an electrical insulator. The AV node and Bundle of His form the only conducting bridge, ensuring the atria contract before the ventricles begin.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Chordae tendineae</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Chordae tendineae are fibrous cords that anchor valve leaflets to papillary muscles. They are structural elements, not electrical conductors.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The fibrous skeleton blocks all direct electrical conduction between atria and ventricles. Only the AV node and Bundle of His penetrate this barrier, creating the sole electrical link."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. This electrical isolation by the fibrous skeleton is what allows the precise sequential timing of atrial and ventricular contraction."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
