          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>The AV node delays the cardiac impulse by approximately 0.1 seconds. What is the</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>The AV node delays the cardiac impulse by approximately 0.1 seconds. What is the purpose of this delay?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>To allow the coronary arteries to fill during diastole</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Coronary filling during diastole is determined by the overall cardiac cycle timing, not specifically by the AV node delay.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>To allow the atria to finish emptying before ventricular contraction begins</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The 0.1-second delay at the AV node ensures the atria complete their contraction and empty blood into the ventricles before ventricular systole begins, maximising cardiac output.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>To prevent the Purkinje fibres from conducting too rapidly</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Purkinje fibres are designed for rapid conduction across the ventricles. The AV delay serves a mechanical coordination purpose, not an electrical protection one.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>To synchronise the heart rate with the respiratory cycle</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Sinus arrhythmia (heart rate variation with breathing) is mediated by autonomic input to the SA node, not by the AV node delay.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The AV node's 0.1-second delay has one critical job: giving the atria time to finish emptying into the ventricles before ventricular contraction begins."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. This brief delay is crucial — it ensures optimal ventricular filling before each contraction."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
